# Literal translation: But when the artichoke blooms and the clear-voiced cicada, sitting in a tree, pours down its shrill song continually from under its wings, in the season of wearisome summer, then goats are fattest and wine is best, women are most wanton, and men are weakest, since Sirius parches head and knees, and skin is dry from the heat;

